        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Spend on the hardware and buy the slab to suit your budget. A quality track and roller set will make a modest door feel expensive, while cheap hardware will make a beautiful door feel like a mistake every single time you open it.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            And measure before you fall in love with a door. The wall space beside the opening, the header above it, and the framing behind the drywall decide whether this project is straightforward or whether it involves opening up a wall — and it is much better to know that first.
          </p>
        </div>

